.TH HASHSUM 1
.SH NAME
hashsum \\- create and verify multi-algorithm file manifests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashsum
hashsum create [--from-jwalk] [--root DIRECTORY] [--output MANIFEST]
.br
[--workers NUMBER] [--progress] [--format json|ndjson] [PATH ...]
.br
hashsum verify --root DIRECTORY [--unexpected] [--format json|ndjson] MANIFEST
.SH DESCRIPTION
Computes SHA-256 and BLAKE3 through one read per file, records unstable reads, and verifies manifest paths safely below a root.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBhashsum --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
